    <h2>Stackburger vs. Classic Burger — What's the Difference?</h2>
    <p>DQ uses the term "Stackburger" for its premium burger line, which distinguishes them from the classic Original Cheeseburger. Key differences:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Stackburgers</strong> are made to order with fresh toppings, higher-quality ingredient combinations, and bolder flavor profiles. They are priced $8.29–$10.87.</li>
      <li><strong>Original Cheeseburger &amp; Double</strong> are the everyday, value-oriented options with standard toppings. The Original Cheeseburger at $6.39 is also available in the $7 Meal Deal.</li>
      <li>Both lines use 100% real seasoned beef, never frozen.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>DQ Burger Nutrition Comparison</h2>
    <p>If you're watching calories, here's how the options stack up from lightest to heaviest:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Grilled Chicken Sandwich — 390 cal (lightest full sandwich option)</li>
      <li>Original Cheeseburger — 400 cal</li>
      <li>Classic Hot Dog — 330 cal (lightest overall)</li>
      <li>Crispy Chicken Sandwich — 470 cal</li>
      <li>Double Cheeseburger — 560 cal</li>
      <li>Two Cheese Deluxe Stackburger — 630 cal</li>
      <li>Mushroom Swiss Stackburger — 680 cal</li>
      <li>Backyard Bacon Ranch Stackburger — 730 cal</li>
      <li>Loaded A.1.® Steakhouse Burger — 760 cal</li>
      <li>FlameThrower® Signature Stackburger — 780 cal (highest)</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>DQ Meal Deals Featuring Burgers</h2>
    <p>The Original Cheeseburger is the entree in the <strong>$7 Meal Deal</strong> — DQ's best-value combo that includes the cheeseburger plus Regular Fries, a Soft Drink, and a Small Sundae for $7.00 all day at participating locations. If you're ordering a burger, check whether the $7 Meal Deal applies before ordering à la carte.</p>
    <p>The <strong>2-for-$5 Mix &amp; Match</strong> also includes the Original Cheeseburger as one of the eligible items — you can pair it with Regular Fries, a Small Sundae, or a Soft Drink for $5.00 total.</p>

